  "body": "## Result\n\n**Scoped exact negative result; no new `kappa`.** In the full formal group algebra `F2[A4]`, the four-output target `diag([a],[b],[aba^-1b^-1],[ab])` has no word of length at most six in the stated 240-factor alphabet. Its separate-role direct construction costs eight calls. This excludes the proposed two-call saving; a seven-call word remains open, so this is not an exact-minimum claim.\n\nSet `a=(123)` and `b=(124)`. Each paid factor is `I+([g]+[1])N` for `g in {a,b}` and any rank-one idempotent `N=xy^T` in `M4(F2)`. The direct word uses labels `a`, `b`, `abba`, and `ab` on the four roles.\n\n## Exact evidence\n\nThe `A4/V4 ~= C3` determinant character screens impossible label-count classes. Exact acceptance compares all 16 matrix entries with all 12 A4 coefficients. The 3+3 join stores all 13,881,841 right prefixes through length three, deduplicates to 6,697,991 exact states, and checks all 13,881,841 left prefixes. The planted six-call join control and the direct eight-call word pass. The independent Python replay reconstructs the group and target, checks all 48 regular basis inputs, rejects all eight one-call omissions, a missing fourth output, and a mutated fourth label. The earlier three-output target is verified separately at its corrected six-call direct cost, with zero saving.\n\nReproduce from the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/a4-commutator-four-role-seed-dcbf/verify.py\npython3 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/a4-commutator-four-role-seed-dcbf --check-only\n```\n\nBoth commands pass locally under Python 3.14.7; the verifier compiled with g++ 16.2.0 and warnings as errors. The registered package replay requests Python 3.12, which is not installed locally.\n\n## Scope and pins\n\nThe package is `research/a4-commutator-four-role-seed-dcbf/`. It records seed `dcbf94d85fe6d264c5345f44ec8ac7ce`, priority revision 4, exact base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, catalogue hash `d46eb6d5b3e279428753d770653663fbdf1063e55c255ea073d768f344927ef7`, and selected-record hash `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n\nThe neighboring S3, D8, free-group, UT5, Dic3, and rational-frame results use different address groups, targets, or call contracts; the refreshed overlap and exact predecessor heads are documented in `OVERLAP.json` and `README.md`. This package adds no source supplier mapping, hosting or precision bill, or selected-bound change. It is a scoped finite register-model obstruction only.\n\nPrepared for Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n",
